  "adaptations": {
    "RTS-02-01": "Continuous1s tick replaces plotting phases. Hits collected inside each tick, primary damage and ordinary critical ratio resolved together; attacks already eligible during that tick remain eligible.",
    "RTS-14-01": "For heterogeneous hits in a tick, ordinary criticals are assigned to contributing hits weighted by primary DP; independent automatic and airframe criticals retain their own source.",
    "RTS-14-02": "No unprinted +/-15% hull variance or blanket per-hit critical probability. Source annex profiles determine target-specific DP.",
    "RTS-07-01": "PRH gen3 can retune to another active radar on the same target. Silent targets are approached at the last emitter position. Its shutdown hit modifier is not inferred from gen2: a terminal event requiring this unresolved value is saved as pending adjudication, without rolling a hit/miss. See R-027.",
    "RTS-14-03": "Aggregate damage-control reduction is distributed proportionally across individual fire/flood records. Each retains its original first-damage deadline, so a later casualty cannot drain HP early or reset an older fire.",
    "RTS-04-01": "A high/very-high missile profile starts at a representative altitude inside the printed band; airborne movement is continuous and terminal transition uses the annex distance/speed. Airframe altitude above the launching aircraft is missile flight, not aircraft ceiling.",
    "RTS-14-04": "For point-platform torpedo collisions, a seeded D3 chooses fore/mid/aft void area independently on each side. A supplied impact_area overrides it. Each area protects once; total side absorption and per-hit R/3 caps remain as printed. This is an explicit spatial abstraction, not a table from the manual.",
    "RTS-14-05": "TPS overflow flooding uses twice the remaining protection as the full-flood threshold, following the worked Enterprise 97DP/24DP example in English14-5/14-6; the surrounding wording is registered in R-025.",
    "RTS-14-06": "Bridge casualty delays a new navigation order (including its route/station) once by two tactical turns. Continuous steering inside the accepted route is not re-delayed each second. Disabled rudder reduces the continuous angular rate to one-third, preserving the printed45-to15-degree ratio.",
    "RTS-14-07": "Secondary fire/flood DP enters the same tick ledger and produces normal ratio criticals. Fire uses the target surface/aviation column; flooding uses the underwater column (submerged submarines use major). Causal immediate flooding is resolved after its initiating hit inside the same tick.",
    "RTS-14-08": "The current instant-spawn deck model stores ready and cycling inventory in the hangar until launch. Hangar hits draw uniformly from this stored inventory, never airborne aircraft. There are no parked-flight-deck locations yet; armed/closely-parked aircraft optional chains are not enabled.",
    "RTS-14-09": "A weapon fit containing multiple physical mounts loses only the selected mount. Remaining pooled ammunition is distributed evenly at the time of the hit; a hit on an already destroyed mount is ignored. Explosion outcome requires explicit topside/belowdecks metadata, otherwise the missing-location adjudication is logged as blocked.",
    "RTS-02-02": "Within a tick, preserve each side command order, apply navigation/emission orders before manual Fire, and collect Blue then Red deterministically. Primary damage remains simultaneous. This removes cross-side input interleaving from projectile allocation and RNG.",
    "RTS-14-10": "Small-craft twice-DP sinking threshold uses a rolling180-second tactical-duration window, including primary and secondary damage. Hull DP does not accumulate outside this window. This preserves the printed tactical duration without introducing arbitrary fixed-turn boundary exploits."
  },
